/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate28_vp_methylDiEthanolAmine -- the vapour pressure of methylDiEthanolAmine, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 steps 2 and 3).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate
  vp methylDiEthanolAmine`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je060269j                 9 pts  519.7-738.4 K  VonNiederhausern; Wilson; Giles
      10.1021/je400373d                 7 pts  467.34-520.28 K  Yang; Feng; Cheng; Zhang et al.
      10.1021/je800290k                 7 pts  409.69-435.5 K  Kim; Svendsen; Borresen
      10.1021/acs.jced.8b00054          6 pts  430.52-488.42 K  Soames; Helal; Iglauer; Barifcani et al.
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2010.08.026: j.fluid.2010.08.026.xml: 1 of 1 pressure rows of methylDiEthanolAmine declare no stated uncertainty -- a partial uncertainty is no uncertainty for a held-out band.  Nothing was written.

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/je060269j (9 pts, 519.7-738.4 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1021/je400373d (7 pts,
  467.34-520.28 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 2.3 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 7 points (1.97 to 2.5 %, mean 2.239 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 520.15 K lies INSIDE the measured span 467.34-738.4 K: the held-out verdict is the test there, no further condition.

  OBJECTIVE (C281 step 3, declared): `objective { method twoStage; }` --
  Vitor's fitting practice (DEV.md 4c C280): least squares in log10 P for a
  first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in P, (P_model - P)/P, over
  the fit points minimised from it; both answers are kept in the result.  A
  student who prefers another objective declares `leastSquares` or `minimax`.

  EARLIER FIT, SUPERSEDED BY THIS DECLARATION
  @@EARLIER-BEGIN@@
  C281 step 2, objective leastSquares (log10 P), the same partition and
  band: WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.717858 - 2013.4423/(T + -93.3716),
  in-sample R2 0.999965 over 9 points, 519.7-738.4 K. HELD OUT: 7 points,
  AAD 5.1341 % against the band 2.3 % -> notValidated. Its own normal
  boiling point (101.325 kPa): 520.66 K. NOT PROMOTED: held-out verdict
  notValidated (AAD 5.134 % against the band 2.3 % declared before the
  fit); the record keeps AmbroseWalton
  @@EARLIER-END@@

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  (filled in by bin/choupo-curate after the run)
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  methylDiEthanolAmine;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylDiEthanolAmine-vapourPressure-je060269j.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je060269j"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylDiEthanolAmine-vapourPressure-je400373d.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je400373d"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  2.3 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 7 points (1.97 to 2.5 %, mean 2.239 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        objective  { method twoStage; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
